.TH G-UNITY7-CLEANUP 8 "November 2026" "g-unity7-desktop" "G Unity7"
.SH NAME
g-unity7-cleanup \- remove the packages of Ubuntu Unity that G Unity7 replaces
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B g-unity7-cleanup
.RB [ \-n | \-\-dry\-run ]
.RB [ \-y | \-\-yes ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B g-unity7-cleanup
removes the duplicate applications of Ubuntu Unity and the other installed
alternatives of the applications of
.BR g-unity7-desktop ,
as
.B emerge \-\-depclean
of Gentoo does.
.PP
The installer of Ubuntu Unity installs the
.B ubuntu-unity-desktop
task and apt marks its packages as manually installed, so
.B apt autoremove
never removes them. apt also keeps every installed alternative of a relation
such as
.BR "showtime | vlc" .
.PP
The script marks
.BR ubuntu-unity-desktop ,
the packages it depends on or recommends that
.B g-unity7-desktop
does not use and their dependencies of the task as automatically installed.
It removes the installed alternatives after the first one of the relations of
.B g-unity7-desktop
if the first one is installed and the alternative is automatically installed
or of the task. An alternative the user installed is kept, as a package of
@world, and so is an alternative other packages need. The packages autoremove
removes then are removed as well.
.PP
It shows all packages and asks for confirmation. To keep one of them, mark it
as manually installed first:
.BI "sudo apt-mark manual " package
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Only show the packages, change nothing. It does not need root.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Do not ask for confirmation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apt (8),
.BR apt-mark (8)
